  "summary": "The generic engineering doctrine as a NORMATIVE TREE, published as a doctrine bundle beside the kit: four cardinals (one case never defines the system; source facts are immutable; under uncertainty, refuse; proven, not claimed), thirteen doctrines and their rules, each with an RFC 2119 modality and, for a MUST, its enforcer. A host answers each address with a stance -- extends to tighten, narrows only with an exception -- and `check` holds the tree coherent (FF-NORMS).",
